# Spec-Driven Workflow

Follow this order strictly. Do not skip steps.

```
Requirement → Specification → Plan/Tasks → Implementation → Testing → Review → Fix
```

## Before Implementation

1. Read relevant files under `spec/` before writing code.
2. If behaviour is not specified, update the spec first — do not guess in code.
3. Do not prompt or implement "build the complete application" in one shot.

## During Implementation

- Make small, reviewable changes aligned with `spec/api-contract.md` and `spec/data-model.md`.
- Enforce the ticket state machine in the backend only (`spec/state-machine.md`).
- Validate all input on the backend; return structured errors the UI can display.
- Never commit secrets, credentials, or `.env` files.

## After Implementation

- Add or update tests per `spec/test-strategy.md`.
- Run `/review-code` before considering work complete.
- Log prompts in `docs/prompt-history.md` and AI mistakes in `docs/ai-mistakes-log.md`.
